<p>When more than one default setting is defined with the same name, GitHub uses the most specific default setting. For example, a default setting defined in a job will override a default setting that has the same name defined in a workflow.</p>
<h2 id="defaultsrunworking-directory" tabindex="-1"><a class="heading-link" href="#defaultsrunworking-directory"><code>defaults.run.working-directory</code><span class="heading-link-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></h2>
<p>Use <code>working-directory</code> to define the working directory for the <code>shell</code> for a step. This keyword can reference several contexts. For more information, see <a href="/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/contexts#context-availability">Contexts</a>.</p>
